# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yifan Cao et al. (2025). Capturing short-range order in high-entropy alloys with machine learning potentials.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-025-01722-2  arXiv:2401.06622v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2401.06622v2 (sha256 8a2e9e5ba3bde3ef...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 564 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/cao2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: MTP ensembles (5 A cutoff; capacities levmax 6-20;
# 20 independent potentials per setting) trained on training sets TS-0
# to TS-5 and the final TS-f for CrCoNi; the liquid energy RMSEs stated
# for TS-0 and TS-3. Warren-Cowley parameters, liquid stability,
# stacking-fault and phase-stability results are properties.

